+# Request 12-057: images of labeled media
+
+STL01–STL03 · November 15, 2026. The individually retrieved public archive member `NIST_FOIA_12-057-DISCS.pdf` contains eight image-only pages with two photographed discs on each page. This is a copy from a third-party archive, not an authenticated agency production or the contents of the photographed discs.
+
+## What the images show
+
+- Physical PDF page **1** shows two discs marked `FOIA # 12-057`, with printed descriptions `FEMA Photos from CD` and `FEMA Video from CD`.
+- Physical PDF pages **2–8** each show two discs with the printed description `FEMA Video from Tapes`. Their handwritten sequence labels run from **1 of 14** through **14 of 14**, in page order.
+
+The inspection was of the page images and labels. The source contains no machine-extractable text. The labels do not prove what is on a disc, that the discs are complete or readable, that the PDF documents all material supplied under the request, or that any particular photo depicts WTC 7 steel. The photographed media and their chain of custody were not inspected. The earlier W14 field-attribution and NIST inventory descriptions remain separate and unresolved.
+
+## Acquisition and remaining work
+
+The member was retrieved from the [public 911datasets archive](https://archive.org/download/911datasets/NIST_FOIA_12-057_Feb_07_2012.zip), rather than downloading the full ZIP. Its exact member path is `NIST_FOIA_12-057_Feb_07_2012/NIST_FOIA_12-057-DISCS.pdf`. The central directory lists 2,210,608 uncompressed bytes and CRC-32 `5d6fcf66`; the retrieved member matched both and has SHA-256 `dbaa9b5cac694827aec69ea876a6d9799e89c4396830ea6b524ddecd56baab9a`. Source/offset and access details are in [SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json). Matching an archive index checks retrieval integrity, not agency authenticity.
+
+The agency response and release manifest, actual disc contents and hashes, source photograph files, field notes, specimen identifiers, and later transfers remain TODOs. A verifiable file-level and item-level join would be required before using any image to test W14A/W14B or NIST's classifications. [Earlier request-log and index observations](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/d9db38c5c88b5ae21b06ac502cd0ddf138274252/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-bpat-request-log-2011-2026-11-15/README.md) remain preserved.
